### A.2 Trust Update Mechanism: Extended Beta Model

The core trust dynamics follow the Guo & Yang (2020) Bayesian framework [[39]][[42]], extended with cultural, regulatory, and cognitive modifiers:

**Base Update Rule:**
$$\alpha_{t+1} = \alpha_t + w \cdot O_t \quad ; \quad \beta_{t+1} = \beta_t + w \cdot (1 - O_t)$$

where $O_t \in \{0,1\}$ is the observed interaction outcome (1=success, 0=failure).

**Weight Modulation Function:**
$$w_{i,r,t} = w_0 \cdot \underbrace{(1 + \lambda_{\text{err}} \cdot e_j)}_{\text{error acknowledgment}} \cdot \underbrace{(1 + \lambda_{\text{reg}} \cdot c_{j,t})}_{\text{regulatory premium}} \cdot \underbrace{\exp(-\gamma \cdot \text{anx}_{i,t} \cdot (1 + \text{Security}_i))}_{\text{anxiety discount}} \cdot \underbrace{(1 + \delta_{i,r} \cdot \mathbb{I}_{\text{bias}})}_{\text{automation bias}}$$

| Parameter | Baseline Value | Source/Calibration | Interpretation |
|-----------|---------------|-------------------|----------------|
| $w_0$ | 1.0 | Guo & Yang (2020) baseline | Base learning rate |
| $\lambda_{\text{err}}$ | 0.3 | HRI error-reporting literature meta-analysis | Bonus for robot error acknowledgment |
| $\lambda_{\text{reg}}$ | 0.4 | Calibrated to EU AI Act certification effect size | Trust premium for certified robots |
| $\gamma$ | 0.8 | RAS validation studies [[50]][[57]] | Anxiety discount steepness |
| $\delta_{i,r}$ | 0.2 (elderly+social), 0.05 (otherwise) | Stock-Homburg & Nguyen (2023/2026) automation bias findings | Automation bias amplification |
| $p_{\text{bias}}$ | 0.15 (elderly+social), 0.02 (otherwise) | Empirical automation bias prevalence in geriatric HRI | Probability of bias-triggered misattribution |

**Mean Trust Estimate:**
$$\bar{T}_{i,r,t} = \frac{\alpha_{i,r,t}}{\alpha_{i,r,t} + \beta_{i,r,t}}$$

**Trust Stability Metric (for H1 testing):**
$$\sigma_{\text{trust},i} = \text{SD}\left(\{\bar{T}_{i,r,t} : t \in [T-365, T]\}\right)$$

### A.3 Anxiety Dynamics Equation

$$\text{anx}_{i,t+1} = \text{clamp}\Big( \text{anx}_{i,t} + \eta \cdot f_{\text{exp},t} \cdot (1 + 0.5 \cdot \text{Security}_i) - \zeta \cdot F_{i,t} - \mu \cdot \bar{c}_{i,t}, \ 0, \ 1 \Big)$$

| Term | Parameter | Value | Rationale |
|------|-----------|-------|-----------|
| Exposure increment | $\eta$ | 0.02 | Calibrated to RAS longitudinal studies |
| Familiarity decay | $\zeta$ | 0.03 | Logistic familiarity gain parameter $\kappa=0.05$ |
| Certification buffer | $\mu$ | 0.04 | EU AI Act anxiety-reduction effect |
| Familiarity function | $F_{i,t} = 1 - \exp(-\kappa \cdot N_{\text{success},i,t})$ | $\kappa=0.05$ | Diminishing-returns learning curve |

### A.4 Autonomy Degradation Function

$$\text{aut}_{i,t} = 100 \cdot \exp\left( - \phi \cdot \frac{d_{\text{sector},t}}{d_{\text{baseline}}} \right) \cdot (1 + 0.5 \cdot \bar{c}_{i,t})$$

- $\phi = 0.01$: Degradation elasticity parameter
- $d_{\text{sector},t}$: Robot density (robots per 1,000 workers) in agent's sector at time *t*
- Certification buffer: 50% reduction in degradation rate when interacting with EU AI Act-certified robots

### A.5 Socratic Debiasing Trigger and Intervention

**Trigger Condition (evaluated daily for agents aged ≥60):**
$$\text{trigger}_{i,t} = \mathbb{I}\left( \max_{r} \bar{T}_{i,r,t} > \theta_{\text{over}} \ \land \ \text{dep}_{i,t} > 0.7 \ \text{for} \ k \ \text{consecutive days} \ \land \ \text{inoc}_{i,t}=0 \right)$$

**Calibrated Parameters (from pilot sweep, Section 7.3):**
- $\theta_{\text{over}} = 0.85$: Overtrust threshold
- $k = 7$ days: Persistence requirement (14 days for elderly agents)

**Intervention Protocol:**
1. Reset trust priors: $\alpha \leftarrow 1, \beta \leftarrow 5$ (skeptical prior, mean ≈ 0.167)
2. Set inoculation flag: $\text{inoc}_{i,t} \leftarrow 1$ for 365 simulated days
3. Reduce automation bias: $\delta_{i,r} \leftarrow \delta_{i,r} / 2$ (permanent)
4. Immediate behavioral adjustment: $\text{dep}_{i,t} \leftarrow \text{dep}_{i,t} - 0.3$

### A.6 Media Framing Shock Implementation

**Monthly Event Generation:**
- Positive frame: probability = 0.4
- Negative frame: probability = 0.3  
- No event: probability = 0.3

**Effect Sizes from Brauner et al. (2026) Pre-registered Experiment [[60]][[61]]:**

| Frame Type | ΔRisk (standardized) | ΔBenefit (standardized) | Model R² |
|------------|---------------------|------------------------|----------|
| Positive | -0.21 | +0.52 | 0.715 |
| Negative | -0.69 | +0.38 | 0.583 |
| Interaction (Risk×Benefit) | β = -0.32 (negative frame only) | — | — |

**Shock Decay Function:**
$$\Delta_{i,\text{current}} = \Delta_{i,\text{initial}} \cdot \exp\left(-\frac{\ln(2)}{15} \cdot \text{days\_since\_event}\right)$$

Half-life = 15 days; shocks modulate the trust weight $w$ multiplicatively.

### A.7 Labor-Market Transition Probabilities

**Daily Separation Probability:**
$$p_{\text{sep},i,t} = p_{\text{base, sector}} + \beta_{\text{robot}} \cdot \Delta d_{\text{sector},t} + \beta_{\text{EPL}} \cdot \text{EPL\_index}_{\text{city}} + \beta_{\text{age}} \cdot \text{age}_i$$

